                                "sense_id": "adc897db-206e-3593-8185-84637caf61d4",
                                "text": "Near-synonyms: artilleryman, artillerywoman, gunner, bombardier"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5e1ef73e-827f-4246-8208-ae425cccdde1",
                                "sense_id": "adc897db-206e-3593-8185-84637caf61d4",
                                "text": "Pelham was, in spite of his youth, an artillerist of the first order of excellence, and his loss was a serious one, in spite of his inferior rank."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2552a48c-9d8c-41a0-ae23-1564c158898c",
                                "sense_id": "adc897db-206e-3593-8185-84637caf61d4",
                                "text": "The experiments were not very satisfactory. Mr. Coffin, perhaps, possibly, because he was not a skilled artillerist, had the mortifying experience of seeing the apparatus in front of his cannon blown into fragments, but he made notes of the other reports."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
